//! The `will-change` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property enables
//! optimizing animations by providing a rendering hint to a browser about how an element is expected
//! to change.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Indicates that the browser applies whatever heuristics and optimizations it normally
//! does. This is the default value.
//! - contents: Specifies that the element's contents, including all the elements in its subtree, are
//! expected to change in the near future, indicating the browser can cache the element less
//! aggressively.
//! - scroll-position: Indicates that the author expects to animate or change the scroll position of
//! the element in the near future.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <animateable-feature>#
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-will-change-1/#propdef-will-change
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/will-change
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

